# Secrets. This repo had NO .gitignore at all, so anything dropped into .env
# went straight to GitHub. A service key, RUN_JOB_KEY or Slack bot token added
# there would have been published automatically with no warning. That is what
# this file is for.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ .env ITSELF IS DELIBERATELY STILL TRACKED — DO NOT UNTRACK IT YET.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are BUILD-TIME values. Vite bakes
# them into the bundle when Cloudflare builds, and Cloudflare builds from a
# clean git clone. Remove .env from the repo and that build gets nothing:
# `isShared` in store.js goes false, the whole Hub silently falls back to this
# browser's localStorage, and every tool opens EMPTY and saves nothing anyone
# else can see. Confirmed live: the current bundle carries the project URL, so
# the build really does depend on this file.
#
# To untrack it safely, in this order:
#   1. Add both VITE_ vars as build variables on the Cloudflare worker.
#   2. Deploy once and confirm the new bundle still contains the project URL.
#   3. Only then `git rm --cached .env`.
# Both keys are publishable by design, so tracking them costs little. Rotating
# the anon key is still worth doing since it sat in git history.
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output and dependencies. Untracked until now only by luck.
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# `wrangler dev` scratch: miniflare's local KV and cache as sqlite, plus a temp
# bundle per run. Machine-local, regenerated every run, and nothing in it is
# production data. Missing until Aug 12 2026 only because nobody had run the
# Worker locally in this repo — the setup notes use the Cloudflare dashboard,
# not the CLI. The first local run drops ~20 untracked files in the root.
.wrangler/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
